# Cloudflare Workers static-assets redirects
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/redirects/
#
# Format: <source> <destination> <status>
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom; the first match wins.
#
# IMPORTANT: only relative URLs are allowed here. Unlike Cloudflare Pages,
# Workers rejects absolute destinations and fails the whole deploy with
# "Only relative URLs are allowed [code: 100324]" - so no rule in this file
# may start with a scheme or hostname.
#
# That means www -> apex CANNOT live here. It is handled by a zone-level
# Redirect Rule instead, which is faster anyway (it runs at the edge before
# the Worker) and is documented in the README under Domain configuration.

# Section moves. Keep these so any link that was already shared, indexed or
# bookmarked still resolves.
#
# The garage moved under Life. The splat rule covers the hub itself (empty
# splat) and both sub-pages in one line. The bare /garage rule is separate
# because a splat pattern does not match the path without its trailing
# slash.
/garage/*      /life/garage/:splat        301
/garage        /life/garage/              301

# The motorcycle page was top-level before it moved under the garage. These
# point straight at the final URL rather than chaining through /garage/, so
# there is only ever one redirect to follow.
/motorcycle/*  /life/garage/motorcycle/:splat  301
/motorcycle    /life/garage/motorcycle/        301
